    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist: Multi-Node Language-Model Serving System\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel sharding across nodes) behaves correctly under controlled conditions. It is designed to catch silent failures \u2014 partial participation, stale configurations, dropped requests, and measurement artifacts \u2014 that do not necessarily produce visible errors.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove every node is running the exact same logical deployment.\n\n- [ ] **Model artifact hash.** Record SHA-256 of model weights, tokenizer files, and config files on every node (or verify via the artifact store's content-addressed URI). Mismatched weights across TP/EP ranks produce silently wrong outputs, not crashes.\n- [ ] **Code/build identity.** Record the serving binary/framework version, git SHA (if built from source), and container image digest on each node. Confirm all digests are identical.\n- [ ] **Sharding plan consistency.** Verify the parallelism configuration (TP degree, PP degree, EP degree, DP replicas, world size) matches the intended topology on every rank. Confirm `world_size = TP \u00d7 PP \u00d7 EP \u00d7 DP` (or your framework's actual product) and that the launcher launched exactly that many ranks.\n- [ ] **Quantization/dtype agreement.** Confirm dtype (fp16/bf16/int8/fp8) and any quantization config are identical across ranks. Mixed precision across TP ranks is a classic silent-corruption source.\n- [ ] **KV cache / memory config.** Record `max_num_seqs`, `max_model_len`, KV cache block counts, and memory fractions per node. Divergent values cause inconsistent admission behavior across DP replicas.\n- [ ] **Sampling parameter defaults.** Verify default temperature, top-p, seed handling, and stop conditions are configured identically where they should be.\n- [ ]",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
